{number: 7}
{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] Crown Him with [Bm] many crowns, the [G] Lamb up-[A] on His [D] throne;
Hark! [D] how the [F#m] heavenly [G] anthem [E7] drowns all [A] music but its own:
A-[D] wake, my [G] soul, and [E7] sing of [A] Him Who died for thee,
And [D] hail Him [G] as thy [D] matchless [G] King through [D] all e-[A7] terni-[D] ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D] Crown Him the [Bm] Lord of love; be-[G] hold His [A] hands and [D] side,
Rich [D] wounds, yet [F#m] visible [G] a-[E7] bove, in [A] beauty glorified:
No [D] angel [G] in the [E7] sky can [A] fully bear that sight,
But [D] downward [G] bends his [D] burning [G] eye at [D] mysteries [A7] so [D] bright.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D] Crown Him the [Bm] Lord of life, Who [G] triumphed [A] o’er the [D] grave,
And [D] rose vic-[F#m] torious [G] in the [E7] strife for [A] those He came to save;
His [D] glories [G] now we [E7] sing, Who [A] died, and rose on high,
Who [D] died, e-[G] ternal [D] life to [G] bring, and [D] lives, that [A7] death may [D] die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[D] Crown Him the [Bm] Lord of heaven, en-[G] throned in [A] worlds a-[D] bove;
Crown [D] Him the [F#m] King, to [G] Whom is [E7] given the [A] wondrous name of Love:
Crown [D] Him with [G] many [E7] crowns, as [A] thrones before Him fall,
Crown [D] Him, ye [G] kings, with [D] many [G] crowns, for [D] He is [A7] King of [D] all.
{end_of_verse}
